{"duration_api_ms": 56817, "stop_reason": "end_turn", "session_id": "04cdd8dc-a98f-4fc1-9386-75d6b40859ff", "total_cost_usd": 0.1149998, "usage": {"input_tokens": 114, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 29288, "cache_read_input_tokens": 320678, "output_tokens": 4626, "output_tokens_details": {"thinking_tokens": 784}, "server_tool_use": {"web_search_requests": 0, "web_fetch_requests": 0}, "service_tier": "standard", "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 29288, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "inference_geo": "not_available", "iterations": [{"input_tokens": 8, "output_tokens": 1308, "cache_read_input_tokens": 36442, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 956, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 956}, "type": "message"}], "speed": "standard"}, "modelUsage": {"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001": {"inputTokens": 1151, "outputTokens": 4641, "cacheReadInputTokens": 320678, "cacheCreationInputTokens": 29288, "webSearchRequests": 0, "costUSD": 0.1149998, "contextWindow": 200000, "maxOutputTokens": 32000, "thinkingTokens": 784, "canonicalModel": "claude-haiku-4-5", "provider": "firstParty", "costBasis": "list"}}, "permission_denials": [], "terminal_reason": "completed", "fast_mode_state": "off", "fast_mode_disabled_reason": "sdk_opt_in_required", "subagent_stats": {"spawned": 0, "requested": {"background": 0, "foreground": 0, "unset": 0}, "started_in_background": 0, "max_depth": 0, "spawned_by_subagents": 0, "completed": 0, "failed": 0, "killed": {"parent": 0, "user": 0, "system": 0}, "refused": {"depth_limit": 0, "concurrency_limit": 0, "budget": 0}, "by_type": {}}, "is_error": false, "num_turns": 24, "subtype": "success", "api_error_status": null, "result": "Based on my review of the repository, here's what an implementer of SPEC.md needs to know:\n\n## Architecture Overview\n\nThe system has three independent export formats from vendors A (Ardent), B (Borough), and C (Calder). Each has a different structure:\n\n**System A (Ardent):**\n- Comment lines prefixed with `#`, then header row, then data rows\n- Columns: `entry_id`, `posted_on` (ISO date), `account`, `memo`, `amount` (dollars with 2 decimals), `currency`\n- Quoted memos supported; current reader rejects them and points to `legacy_parser.py`\n\n**System B (Borough):**\n- Plain header row, then data rows (no preamble/trailer)\n- Columns: `sys` (always \"B\"), `doc_no`, `value_date` (ISO date), `acct`, `descr`, `amount` (integer cents), `cur`\n- **Critical:** Borough writes amounts as integer cents, not dollars. Must call `system_b.to_major_units()` to convert\n\n**System C (Calder):**\n- Banner line \"CALDER EXPORT\", header row, data rows, trailer \"== N rows ==\"\n- Columns: `ref`, `txn_date` (DD/MM/YYYY format — not ISO!), `ledger_acct`, `narrative`, `gross_amount` (dollars with 2 decimals), `ccy`\n- Trailers can miscount; logged as warning but not fatal\n\n## Key Conventions\n\n**Amounts:** Always `decimal.Decimal`, never `float`. System A and C supply dollars; System B supplies cents (divide by 100). Round totals half-to-even via `Decimal.quantize()` (the default mode).\n\n**Dates:** Always `datetime.date`. System A and B are ISO; System C is DD/MM/YYYY. Readers return raw strings; conversion happens at the Record-building layer.\n\n**Output:** The normalized CSV header is fixed:\n```\nrecord_id,source_system,date,account_code,account_name,description,amount\n```\n\n**Accounts:** Code → name via `ledgerkit.mapping.account_name(code, unknown_label)`. Unknown codes get the label from config `[report] unknown_account_label` (default: \"UNCLASSIFIED\").\n\n**Ordering:** Records sort by date (ISO), then source system (A/B/C), then record_id — use `sort_key()` from `ledgerkit.core.records`.\n\n## Configuration & Settings\n\n- Built-in defaults in `ledgerkit.config.DEFAULTS`\n- Checked-in config at `config/settings.toml` (do not modify)\n- Override via `LEDGERKIT_CONFIG` environment variable (layered on top, only changed keys needed)\n- Settings loaded via `load_settings()` with no arguments (reads env var internally)\n- Sections: `[report]` (decimals, unknown_account_label), `[reconcile]` (tolerance), `[validate]` (account_code_pattern)\n\n## Code Boundaries\n\n- **Parsers** (`parsers/*.py`): Read and return raw strings only. Do NOT convert values.\n- **Record-building** (caller's responsibility): Interpret values based on system knowledge, create `Record` objects with converted amounts/dates\n- **`normalize()`**: Cleans, filters, and orders records. Has a `keep_refunds` parameter; defaults to dropping refunds.\n- **`emit()`** in `cli.py` is the only print; everything else logs via `get_logger(__name__)`\n\n## CLI Structure\n\n- Arguments use `argparse`; subcommands via `add_subparsers(dest=\"command\", required=True)`\n- Each command is a handler function that receives `argparse.Namespace` and returns exit code\n- **Important:** `--config` is a global option (given before COMMAND), not per-command; access via `args.config` if present\n- Flag names are fixed in SPEC.md: `--out`, `--by`, `--records`, `--include-refunds`, `--tolerance`, `--config`\n\n## Testing & Validation\n\n- Account code pattern validation via regex in config (default: `^[0-9]{4}$`)\n- Field count checking: must match header count or raise `LedgerParseError`\n- Date format validation per system (ISO for A/B, DD/MM/YYYY for C)\n- Amount parsing: reject non-numeric (System B) or non-Decimal (Systems A/C)\n- `count_data_lines()` in parsers gives raw line count without full parse\n\n## What Implementers Must Do\n\n1. Build converters from raw row dicts to `Record` objects (handle per-system format differences)\n2. Wire five new subcommands into `build_parser()` with correct flag names\n3. Implement `ingest`, `report`, `reconcile`, `validate` commands and handlers\n4. Handle CSV writing with proper quoting via `fields.join_record()` for descriptions\n5. Handle `--config` as a global arg in main parser before subcommands\n6. Ensure all public functions have full type annotations\n7. Use `_log.warning()` for data validation issues, `emit()` for CLI output only\n8. Import settings and logger once at module load; do NOT import `utils.cache` or use `legacy_parser`", "ttft_ms": 2132, "type": "result", "duration_ms": 56585, "uuid": "9fb9fffc-1c9b-415b-b6b5-7980c3119b96", "ttft_stream_ms": 635, "time_to_request_ms": 67, "first_content_frame_ms": 805, "queued_turn_count": 0, "_label": "p1-1-task", "_wall_s": 57.8, "_argv": ["claude", "-p", "--model", "haiku", "--tools", "Read,Write,Edit,Bash,Grep,Glob", "--allowedTools", "Read,Write,Edit,Bash,Grep,Glob", "--disallowedTools", "Agent", "WebFetch", "WebSearch", "--strict-mcp-config", "--setting-sources", "", "--output-format", "json", "--add-dir", "/tmp/claude-1000/-home-anatoly/24e92440-efc2-4a14-97c2-ee126ebf0ca1/scratchpad/ab/topic/S/haiku/topic-r3-topic-b", "--add-dir", "/home/anatoly/llm-intelligence-test/v3/distractors"]}
