ivide by 100 → -88.25\n```\nThe parser has `to_major_units()` for this conversion. The comment warns that two importers have been caught treating these as dollars, getting numbers 100× too large.\n\n**System C (Calder):** Already dollars with 2 decimals as written\n```\n386.54 → use as-is\n```\n\n## Dates\n\n**System A (Ardent):** ISO format, ready to parse\n```\n2026-01-03 → parse as YYYY-MM-DD\n```\n\n**System B (Borough):** ISO format, ready to parse\n```\n2026-01-07 → parse as YYYY-MM-DD\n```\n\n**System C (Calder):** DD/MM/YYYY format — the opposite of the others\n```\n02/01/2026 → must parse as day-first, not month-first\n                → February 1, 2026 (not January 2)\n```\n\nThe parser explicitly warns about this: \"Read month first and the rows past the twelfth of a month blow up, while the rows on or before it quietly land in the wrong month.\" System C's date field is handed on as raw text because the reader doesn't know which system it came from yet.\n\n**Bottom line:** Before ingest normalizes anything, amounts need System B conversion (cents→dollars), and dates need System C conversion (DD/MM/YYYY→ISO). Systems A and C amounts and A/B dates are already in the right form.", "ttft_ms": 11005, "type": "result", "duration_ms": 15623, "uuid": "d6f64c5d-f8fb-40d0-95d5-fa41bed95f22", "ttft_stream_ms": 650, "time_to_request_ms": 95, "first_content_frame_ms": 837, "queued_turn_count": 0, "_label": "p1-3-task", "_wall_s": 17.0, "_argv": ["claude", "-p", "--model", "haiku", "--tools", "Read,Write,Edit,Bash,Grep,Glob", "--allowedTools", "Read,Write,Edit,Bash,Grep,Glob", "--disallowedTools", "Agent", "WebFetch", "WebSearch", "--strict-mcp-config", "--setting-sources", "", "--output-format", "json", "--add-dir", "/tmp/claude-1000/-home-anatoly/24e92440-efc2-4a14-97c2-ee126ebf0ca1/scratchpad/ab/topic/S/haiku/topic-r3-topic-b", "--add-dir", "/home/anatoly/llm-intelligence-test/v3/distractors", "--resume", "04cdd8dc-a98f-4fc1-9386-75d6b40859ff"]}
